## Third-party dependencies

OmaGlass shells out to standard system tools rather than bundling any code.
None of these are distributed with this repository:

- `omarchy-network-status` (part of Omarchy) — interface/link status
- `ss` (iproute2) — socket/connection and byte-counter sampling
- `ip` (iproute2) — LAN neighbor discovery (`ip neigh show`)
- `bash` (`/dev/tcp`) — on-demand IP whois lookups from the Connections tab,
  spoken directly over TCP/43 rather than via a separate `whois` binary
- `getent` (glibc) — reverse-DNS hostname lookups in the Usage tab
- `curl` — batched GeoIP lookups against `ip-api.com`
- `wl-copy` (wl-clipboard) — clipboard copy actions

At runtime, only public IPs you are already connected to are sent (batched)
to `ip-api.com`, a free public GeoIP service; private/local addresses are
never looked up. See the in-app Settings tab for the full data/privacy notes.
